      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "No. 132/2025 against the Petitioner/Accused No.3 for the offence punishable U/S.420, 506 r/w 34 IPC and Sec.3(1)(s), 3(2)(va) of SC/ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Amendment Act, 2015 which is pending before the Hon'ble IV Addl. District & Sessions Judge-cum-Spl. Sessions Court for SC/ST (POA) Act, Guntur AND WHEREAS the High Court upon perusing the petition and memorandum of grounds filed herein and upon hearing the arguments of Sri SRINIVASA RAO NARRA Advocate for the Petitioner, ASSISTANT PUBLIC PROSECUTOR for the Respondent No.1, directed issue of Donthagani Bhargav vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 2 January, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/103421733/\n1 notice to the Respondent No.2 herein to show cause as to why this CRIMINAL PETITION should not be admitted.\nYou viz:\nKancherla Ashok Chandra @ Chanti, S/o. Peter Paul @ Pandu, aged about 35 years,\nR/o. Malapalle, Kollipara Village, Kollipara Mandal, Guntur District, A.P. are be and hereby directed to show cause either appearing in person or through an Advocate, as to why in the circumstances set out in the petition and the memorandum of grounds filed therewith(copy enclosed ) this CRIMINAL PETITION should not be admitted on or before 06.02.2026 to which date the case stands posted for hearing.\nlA NO: 1 OF 2025 Petition under Section 482 of Criminal Procedure code/ Section 528 of BNSS is filed praying that in the circumstances stated in the affidavit filed in support of the petition, the High Court may be pleased to Stay of all further proceedings including trial against the Petitioner/Accused No.3 in S.C. SPL. No. 132/2025 pending before the Hon'ble IV Addl. District &\nSessions Judge- cum-Spl. Sessions Court for SC/ST (POA) Act, Guntur for the offence punishable U/s.420, 506 r/w 34 IPC and Sec.3(1)(s), 3(2)(va) of SC/ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Amendment Act, 2015, pending disposal of CRLP No. 13538 of 2025, on the file of the High Court.",
